@startuml proximity-detection
title US-05: Proximity Detection - Episode model; one candidate per encounter

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:{cell}\n(sorted set,\nwritten by Position Consumer)" as GeoCell
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as LiveState
database "Redis\nproximity-episode:{pair_key}" as Episode
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Alerts
participant "Express API" as API
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as TSDB
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Kafka -> Correlation : consume position event\n{ entity_id, live_geo_cell, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, ... }

note over Correlation
  Position Consumer already wrote the geo-cell sorted set.
  Correlation Worker only reads from it.
  k-ring radius computed from PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES
  and cell edge length at LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION — not hardcoded.
end note

Correlation -> GeoCell : ZRANGEBYSCORE geo-cell:{cell} (now - LIVE_PROXIMITY_MAX_AGE_MS) +inf\n(for each cell in k-ring)
GeoCell --> Correlation : candidate entity IDs (fresh members only)

Correlation -> LiveState : HGETALL entity:live:{candidate_id}\n(for each candidate)
LiveState --> Correlation : { lat, lon, last_seen_ms, ... }

Correlation -> Correlation : recheck last_seen_ms — skip stale candidates\ncompute distance to each fresh candidate

alt distance <= PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES
  note over Correlation
    pair_key = min(entity_id, candidate_id) + ':' + max(entity_id, candidate_id)
    Canonical ordering prevents A:B and B:A being treated as different pairs.
  end note

  Correlation -> Episode : HGETALL proximity-episode:{pair_key}
  Episode --> Correlation : existing episode fields or nil

  alt episode key exists (continuing encounter)
    alt candidate_published == 0 (Kafka publish failed in prior attempt)
      Correlation -> ProxKafka : retry publish proximity.candidates\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }
      Correlation -> Episode : set candidate_published = 1 on success
    end
    Correlation -> Episode : update last_seen_ms = event.timestamp_ms\nrefresh TTL (PROXIMITY_EPISODE_GAP_MS)
    note over Correlation
      Continuing encounter. No new candidate event.
      TTL refresh keeps episode alive while pair stays close.
    end note

  else no active episode (new encounter)
    Correlation -> Neo4j : check for KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge between pair

    alt KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge exists (expected proximity)
      Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge\n(durable evidence — not anomalous)
      Correlation -> Episode : create episode hash (TTL only, no candidate_published)
      note over Correlation
        Known associate — routine proximity.
        Neo4j edge written for historical record.
        Episode hash prevents Neo4j write on every subsequent ping.
        No proximity.candidates event published.
      end note

    else no KNOWN_ASSOCIATE (unscheduled proximity)
      note over Correlation
        episode_start_ms = event.timestamp_ms (source event time)
        Write order: Neo4j → set candidate_published=0 → Kafka → set candidate_published=1
      end note
      Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge\nidempotency_key = {pair_key}:{episode_start_ms}
      Correlation -> Episode : create proximity-episode hash\n{ episode_start_ms, last_seen_ms: event.timestamp_ms,\n  candidate_published: 0 }
      Correlation -> ProxKafka : publish proximity.candidates\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }
      Correlation -> Episode : set candidate_published = 1

      note over ProxKafka
        One proximity.candidates event per episode.
        Alert Evaluator triggered once per encounter.
        If publish fails: candidate_published stays 0;
        retry on next ping for this pair.
      end note
    end
  end
end

== Alert Evaluator - consumes proximity.candidates ==

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

note over Evaluator
  One event per episode — not one per ping.
  Known associates already filtered upstream.
  Checks for signal loss correlation (see US-06).
  If no signal loss: emits UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY.
end note

Evaluator -> Alerts : publish UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY alert

Alerts -> API : consume alert
API -> TSDB : persist alert (idempotent on replay)
API --> Dashboard : push alert over WebSocket\n(scope-matched connections only)
Dashboard --> Operator : proximity alert displayed

@enduml
